1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:01,957
There's one island on Earth where

2
00:00:01,957 --> 00:00:03,714
you're not allowed to set foot...

3
00:00:03,714 --> 00:00:06,500
and the people living there want it that way.

4
00:00:06,500 --> 00:00:08,596
This is North Sentinel Island,

5
00:00:08,596 --> 00:00:10,483
in India's Andaman Islands.

6
00:00:10,483 --> 00:00:13,500
About 60 square kilometres of jungle.

7
00:00:13,500 --> 00:00:15,332
It's home to the Sentinelese,

8
00:00:15,332 --> 00:00:18,176
one of the last uncontacted peoples on Earth.

9
00:00:18,176 --> 00:00:20,600
Nobody knows how many there are.

10
00:00:20,600 --> 00:00:22,376
In 1880, British officers

11
00:00:22,376 --> 00:00:24,080
took a few of them away.

12
00:00:24,080 --> 00:00:26,900
Two reportedly fell sick and died.

13
00:00:26,900 --> 00:00:30,287
Ever since, they've met outsiders with arrows.

14
00:00:30,287 --> 00:00:31,612
Even a helicopter,

15
00:00:31,612 --> 00:00:33,700
after the 2004 tsunami.

16
00:00:33,700 --> 00:00:36,565
So India made the island a protected reserve.

17
00:00:36,565 --> 00:00:38,538
Boats must keep their distance,

18
00:00:38,538 --> 00:00:40,500
and visiting is illegal.

19
00:00:40,500 --> 00:00:42,993
Not just for our safety, but for theirs.

20
00:00:42,993 --> 00:00:45,562
A common cold could wipe them out.

21
00:00:45,600 --> 00:00:47,494
They've chosen to be left alone.

22
00:00:47,494 --> 00:00:49,306
Would you respect that?
